{"kind":"report","text":"Design decision for21664f0f: proceed with A0a and the proposed L1/L3 direction, with the following boundaries. This closes only the requested pre-Source design decision; full e871 durability/archive/live work remains owed.\n\n1. A0a is a partial declaration slice. Keep format artroom-definition-1 and required genesis for recorded definitions. Add the optional exact versioned level shape. An absent member retains its current recorded meaning without adding a property, rewriting retained bytes or changing any existing digest. Explicit recorded@1 is allowed and is its own definition/pin: it is not byte-identical to omission. Reject malformed/extra level members, unknown names and versions. Until their complete execution path exists, live@1 and archived@1 must fail whole-definition admission. Never accept them and run recorded semantics. Prefer the existing validator unsupported-definition problem at path level with a precise message; an internal unsupported-level diagnostic is acceptable only if all public founding/replay responses retain unsupported-definition. Current Founded/Replay contracts do not define public unsupported-level.\n\n2. Preserve the distinction between declaration support and deployment support. A0a does not complete A0: room permission, archive-unavailable, discovery and new platform versions remain owed in A0b. A0b must not enable archived execution merely because permission exists; do so only when the archive executor/backend and required dependencies are ready. Existing rooms and native pins keep their meaning. New room permission must disclose repository-wide readability before consent; it cannot be inferred from a deployment switch or inferred for an old room. Archived-without-permission or destination must refuse archive-unavailable when archived creation becomes implemented, never create an unarchived fallback.\n\n3. L1: use artroom-definition-2 for live definitions and their live forms. Require explicit live@1 there and require genesis to be absent. Retain format1 with required genesis for recorded/archived definitions. Use discriminated types/validation rather than making genesis optional across all definitions. Missing level in format1 remains recorded; missing level in format2 must not silently select live or recorded. Reject unsupported format/level combinations whole. New format2 support does not itself imply a live executor is available. The static live-effect restrictions of16.5 and all live session/generation/result obligations still apply.\n\n4. L3: the directory records establishment in a new version, one item per established live scope, and discovery supplies the bounded host/established/ordinal locator. This follows16.2 and16.6. The locator is routing only. Before minting G, check a real authorized applied establishment entry of the expected kind, its exact host incarnation, signed-intent cause, ordinal, definition and membership binding; rebuild the acyclic seed from intentDigest, not the entry hash, and match the addressed ID. A refused or unrelated entry grants nothing. Missing/mismatched inputs yield unavailable with no state or explanatory disclosure. Start, membership and watch reads share host read admission, including pre-generation reads; preserve L5's line-by-line reconciliation and measured mixed-load witness. Establishment implementation is a later dependent slice, not part of A0a.\n\n5. A1 may proceed independently as a pure layout slice. Its manifest must inventory dependencies by each replay input variant, including outcome snapshots/values and observing-delivery values, and encode explicit privacy omissions. Resolve J1/J2/J9 before claiming complete layout/export. No private bytes, credentials or detached texts may be exported by treating an incomplete inventory as permission.\n\nWitnesses for A0a: pin fidelity for unchanged implicit-recorded definitions; a real explicit-recorded founding retained and replayed under its actual digest; rejected unsupported levels causing no native writes; meaningful malformed/version cases at the validator boundary. Exercise the actual runtime/replay mapping, not just an enum helper. Focused distinguishing controls and one gate at the eventual review head follow docs/testing.md. No new full gate is needed for this design-only report.\n\nBasis: static exact Main0157307b9 reads of the durability note15.1-15.3,15.9-15.10 and16; contract definition.ts18-29; derive validate/index.ts149-161,249-271 and shape.ts47-57; Core.validate318-325 and found429-519; replay verify.ts732-753. They confirm strict top-level refusal today, required recorded genesis, digesting the original declared value, validation before founding writes and unsupported-definition mapping on replay. No project execution, Source edits, tests, gate or provider work was performed. Architecture: preserve the one-level/one-scope boundary and staged support. Security: consent, whole-definition refusal and authenticated establishment are required. Simplification: preserve current recorded paths and public refusal contracts; introduce no fallback executor or second identity system.","body":{"formal_source_approval":"false","head":"0157307b904c9afc75500b626fc565a152113cfa","review_scope":"design-decision-only"}}